#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## 05 Specialization cost: when an improvement pays for itself, when it
## does not, and a rule that is never far from the best.
##
## Run with "just run-exp 05". A deterministic simulation: each task
## kind can be improved once for i = 3000 tokens, which cuts its cost
## from b = 1000 to a = 450 tokens a task (the research's example).
## A workload is how many times each kind recurs. Groups:
##   A      fixed harness: never improves
##   D      always improves: improves every kind before its first task
##   D-ski  cost-aware: improves a kind once it has been done k times at
##          the baseline, k the break-even rounded up (ski rental)
##   best   hindsight: the cheaper choice per kind, knowing its count
##          (not achievable without knowing the future: the yardstick)

"ec:" u_se< "Econ"

s := (3000, 1000, 450)
k := ec:s_kiRental s

### The break-even

"break-even (tasks of one kind):"
ec:b_reakEven s
"the cost-aware rule improves after k baseline tasks, k ="
k

### Repetition swept, 40 tasks in all

## r tasks of each of 40 / r kinds: from all different to all the same.
r := 1 2 4 5 8 10 20 40
kinds := 40 d_iv r
fixed := kinds * s ec:f_ixed r
eager := kinds * s ec:e_ager r
ski := kinds * (3000, 1000, 450, k) ec:a_fter r
best := kinds * s ec:h_indsight r
"uses per kind:"
r
"total tokens, rows A, D, D-ski, best:"
4 8 r_eshape fixed c_at eager c_at ski c_at best
"D against A, percent (above 100 the improving harness costs more):"
f_loor 0.5 + 100 * eager / fixed
"D-ski against best, percent (never above 200):"
f_loor 0.5 + 100 * ski / best

### Four workload shapes

## Each a vector of uses per kind; the totals per group.
u:t_otals := { c -> ('+ r_/ s ec:f_ixed c) c_at ('+ r_/ s ec:e_ager c) c_at ('+ r_/ (3000, 1000, 450, k) ec:a_fter c) c_at '+ r_/ s ec:h_indsight c }
"totals for A, D, D-ski, best; one-off (40 kinds once):"
u:t_otals 40 r_eshape 1
"routine (4 kinds, 10 each):"
u:t_otals 4 r_eshape 10
"heavy tail (most kinds rare, a few common):"
u:t_otals 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 2 2 3 5 8 13 21
"drifting (each kind just short of the break-even):"
u:t_otals 8 r_eshape 5

### A budget, knowing the expected reuse

## The heavy tail again, with at most 9000 tokens to invest: which
## kinds to improve (a mask over the 15 kinds), what that saves, and
## the total cost (the improved kinds at a, the others at b, plus the
## investments).
c := 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 2 2 3 5 8 13 21
n := t_ally c
cands := (n r_eshape 3000, n r_eshape 550, c)
bought := 9000 ec:a_llocate cands
"improved kinds (budget 9000):"
bought
"net saving:"
cands ec:n_et bought
"total tokens with the budget:"
('+ r_/ s ec:f_ixed c) - cands ec:n_et bought
